# UST.G3FE: H02 Component-20 Eight-Prime Graded Promotion Audit Theorem

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_EIGHT_PRIME_GRADED_PROFILE_NUMERIC_PROMOTION_REJECTED_COLON_MODULE_OPEN`

This theorem is exact over eight complete split algebras, comprising 48
canonical fibers. It does not promote the result to `Q(gamma)`.

## Setup

For every archived split prime, UST.G3DI--UST.G3DU provide the canonical
ordered component-20 kernel

```text
K_15 subset Sym^15(k^3),  dim(K_15) = 100.
```

Define the largest graded ideal pieces visible at degree 15 by

```text
I_d = {f in Sym^d(k^3) : f Sym^(15-d)(k^3) subset K_15}.
```

UST.G3FD established the resulting graded presentation at the six roots over
the first split prime. UST.G3FE repeats the construction over all eight
archived split primes and performs a seven-prime construction followed by an
independent eighth-prime holdout.

## Theorem

All 48 split fibers have one common normalized generator profile:

```text
4  minimal generators in degree 11,
15 minimal generators in degree 14,
11 minimal generators in degree 15.
```

Through degree 15, the first syzygies contain exactly

```text
1 linear syzygy in degree 12,
1 new quadratic syzygy in degree 13 modulo the three linear multiples.
```

Consequently, the truncated presentation is

```text
R(-12) + R(-13)
    -> R(-11)^4 + R(-14)^15 + R(-15)^11
    -> I through degree 15,
```

and it gives the exact finite-field Hilbert identities

```text
dim I_11 = 4,
dim I_12 = 4*3 - 1 = 11,
dim I_13 = 4*6 - 3 - 1 = 20,
dim I_14 = 4*10 - 6 - 3 + 15 = 46,
dim I_15 = 4*15 - 10 - 6 + 15*3 + 11 = 100.
```

The same normalization chart is valid on all 48 fibers.

## Numerical-Promotion Decision

The compressed generator payload contains 21,648 power-basis residues per
prime; the compact syzygy payload contains 216. The first seven primes give
the CRT modulus

```text
359164433419006164411572822811067
```

with rational-reconstruction uniqueness bound

```text
13400828956057273.
```

Literal replay at the eighth prime gives:

```text
generator payload:
  17,511 valid candidates,
  10,980 holdout passes,
  10,950 structural zeros,
  30 normalization units,
  0 passing nontrivial coefficients;

syzygy payload:
  157 valid candidates,
  60 holdout passes,
  56 structural zeros,
  4 normalization units,
  0 passing nontrivial coefficients.
```

Thus the only promoted values are coefficients forced by normalization or
support. No genuinely nontrivial normalized coefficient survives the
independent holdout.

