## Consequence

The component-20 kernel is not an unstructured 5,411-coordinate numerical
object. Across all tested split fibers it is the degree-15 part of a compact
graded module with 30 minimal generators and two visible first-syzygy types.
This is a substantial structural reduction.

At the same time, the holdout proves that simply adding more split primes is
not a credible promotion route. The normalized coefficients vary in a way
that is not captured by bounded rational reconstruction in the chosen chart.

## Claim Boundary and Next Object

UST.G3FE does not prove finite-flatness over the characteristic-zero base,
does not reconstruct the generators over `Q(gamma)`, does not prove the
component-20 rank contribution 36 over `Q(gamma)`, and does not close the
global H02 rank.

The next proof object is an exact selected colon module over `Q(gamma)`:

```text
I_d = {f : f Sym^(15-d)
             lies in the ordered prior-source plus Jacobian image}.
```

It must be constructed directly from the G3EX cohomological/Macaulay
presentation and supplied with a degree-through-15 free-resolution proof.
That upstream construction, rather than further blind prime extension, is the
remaining characteristic-zero route.
